<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/infographic-chatbot-development-path.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<div class="n3l-chatbot-development-path">
<figure class="fig">

  <header class="mast">
    <span class="eyebrow brand-eyebrow">NEXT3LABS &mdash; AI chatbot development, Singapore</span>
    <div class="title">The demo takes two weeks. <span class="hi">The build is the rest.</span></div>
    <p class="sub">Connecting a model to a chat window is easy. Making it <strong>reliably right about your business</strong> is the actual project.</p>
    <div class="mast-rule"></div>
  </header>

  <div class="split">
    <div class="half half--demo">
      <span class="eyebrow half-label">What the demo proves</span>
      <p class="half-line">It is <b>fluent</b>, polite and awake at 3am.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="half half--real">
      <span class="eyebrow half-label">What it does not prove</span>
      <p class="half-line">That it is <b class="stop-em">correct</b> about your prices, policies and records.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="steps-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">The build path &mdash; five stages, each with a deliverable</span>
    <span class="legend">Ship stage <i>n</i> before starting <i>n+1</i></span>
  </div>

  <ol class="steps">

    <li class="step">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Scope &mdash; decide what it may answer</h3>
        <p>Sort three months of real enquiries. The repeat questions are the bot&rsquo;s job; the long tail routes to a person.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="out">Answer &amp; hand-over list</span>
    </li>

    <li class="step">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Ground it &mdash; knowledge base first</h3>
        <p>Current pricing, policies, real front-line answers. Every reply traceable to a source document.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="out">Source of truth <b>+ a named owner</b></span>
    </li>

    <li class="step">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Integrate &mdash; website, WhatsApp, your systems</h3>
        <p>&ldquo;Where is my order&rdquo; needs a live read, not a document. Without that, it is an FAQ page with a cursor.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="out">Live reads, with fallbacks</span>
    </li>

    <li class="step step--gate">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Verify &mdash; on real conversations, not your own script</h3>
        <p><b class="gate-em">Grade three things: is it correct, did it escalate when it should, does it sound like you.</b> The wrong answers map the holes.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="out out--gate">A human read of the logs</span>
    </li>

    <li class="step step--last">
      <span class="idx num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
      <div class="body">
        <h3>Launch narrow, watch it, then widen</h3>
        <p>One channel or one question type. Read the transcripts weekly. Hand-over to a person always one tap away.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="out out--done">Monitored, reversible go-live</span>
    </li>

  </ol>

  <section class="fails">
    <span class="eyebrow fails-label">The four ways it dies</span>
    <ul class="fail-list">
      <li class="fail-item"><span class="x" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span><b>Confident wrong answers</b><span>No grounds to answer &mdash; answers anyway.</span></li>
      <li class="fail-item"><span class="x" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span><b>Stale knowledge base</b><span>Right at launch, wrong by next quarter.</span></li>
      <li class="fail-item"><span class="x" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span><b>An FAQ in disguise</b><span>No integrations, so no real answers.</span></li>
      <li class="fail-item"><span class="x" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span><b>Escalation dead end</b><span>The bot becomes the thing to defeat.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <figcaption class="foot">
    <span class="mark-word">NEXT3LABS</span>
    <span>Takes the repetitive questions, not the people &middot; next3labs.com</span>
  </figcaption>

</figure>
</div>
